    "created_at": "2023-10-19T04:40:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-10-19T04:40:07Z",
    "body": "In general it's a bad idea to use `Promise.resolve()`-like behavior because it results in oddities like keeping expando properties, or not converting cases like\r\n\r\n```js\r\nconst promise = Promise.resolve();\r\npromise.then = doSomethingCustom;\r\n```\r\n\r\ninto \"normal\" promises. This is why throughout the web platform we use `new Promise(r => r(webDeveloperValue))` instead.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
